\paragraph{Effect size and downstream impact.}
The in-distribution PPL improvement ($\Delta{=}{-}0.023$ at $\rho{=}0.4$) operates within a narrow residual (${\sim}$0.07-point window between uniform and grid-best), and does not transfer to downstream accuracy: mean accuracy is identical (0.5414 vs.\ 0.5414, 5 seeds, 5 tasks; Appendix~\ref{app:downstream}), consistent with nonlinear PPL-to-accuracy transfer~\citep{tay2023scale,ye2025mixing}.
After accounting for the epoch confound, the paradigm's impact at current scales is modest (Appendix~\ref{app:power}); at $\rho{=}0.6$ the effect roughly doubles ($\Delta{=}{-}0.032$) but this extrapolation is speculative.

